# The commit identities this repository accepts, one shell glob per line.
# Read by BOTH tools/git-hooks/pre-commit and
# tools/check-commit-identities.py, so the hook and the check cannot
# drift apart -- which is the fault this project keeps finding, and the
# reason this is a file rather than two copies of a list.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. An exposure audit found a work email on 3 commits and
# `<account>@<hostname>.lan` on 26 more, in a public repository. Commit
# metadata is published the moment it is pushed and is indexed from
# there, so the only real fix is upstream of the push. This list is that
# fix; the history itself was left alone deliberately, because rewriting
# it changes all 394 SHAs, dangles every SHA citation in these docs, and
# still would not reach anyone's existing clone or fork.
#
# GitHub's own two settings are the stronger half and are not in this
# repository: "Keep my email addresses private" and "Block command line
# pushes that expose my email". The second one would have prevented both
# findings on its own. CONTRIBUTING.md says so.
*@users.noreply.github.com
noreply@github.com
noreply@anthropic.com
